  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "The area of the rectangle is increasing. The base of the rectangle is $b,$ and its height is $10$ times its base. Find the rate of change of the area of a rectangle with respect to its base.",
  "worked_solution": "The area of a rectangle is given by  \n\n$$\nA=bh,\n$$\n\n where $b$ is the base and $h$ is the height of the rectangle.\n\nWe are given that $h=10b,$ so we can express the area $A$ as a function of the base $b$ by substituting $h=10b$ in the formula above. We get\n\n$$\nA=b(10b)=10{b}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(b)$  with respect to $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{\u2032}(b) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}(10{b}^{2}) \\\\  & =10\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}({b}^{2}) \\\\  & =10(2b) \\\\  & =20b.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
